 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+Staff also ask the inverse question, so the clinic publishes a specialty view of the same directory (stated 2026-08-11). It lists every specialty the clinic knows, under the name the clinic stores, and shows the veterinarians holding each one by first name followed by last name. Every specialty appears on a single page. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it, because the view lists specialties rather than the roster `[REQ-VET-003]`. The view only reads; managing veterinarians or specialties remains out of scope (NG-2). It is reached by its own address and by nothing else: no navigation entry and no page of the system links to it. The view itself carries the usual navigation, as every page does.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty view is opened, then every one is listed under its stored name, all on one page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the view is opened, then each holder is shown by first name followed by last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the view is opened, then that veterinarian is not shown anywhere on it.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a reader who requests the view's own address, when the request is made, then the view opens, and no other page offers a link to it.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian shown under it.
+2. When the clinic knows no specialty at all, the view opens empty rather than failing.
+3. The specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+4. Two veterinarians sharing a full name are each listed under every specialty they hold.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
